<title>UK: Dairy Farm H1 profit slips, warns on year.</title>
<headline>Dairy Farm H1 profit slips, warns on year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   ($ million unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (cents)		1.23		   vs 3.20</p>
<p> Dividend (cents)	 1.65		   vs 1.65</p>
<p> Trading profit	   52.9		   vs 86.8</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,337.6		vs 2,981.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     42.9		   vs 80.5</p>
<p>Note - &quot;Earnings in the current year are expected to be lower than in 1995. It is the board's intention, however, to maintain the dividend for the full year at the same level as for 1995,&quot; the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 21.0		   vs 41.4</p>
<p> Net interest expense   10.0		   vs 6.3</p>
<p> Tax			  17.2		   vs 18.7</p>
<p> Net taxed		  28.1		   vs 61.8</p>
<p> Attributable	     21.3		   vs 55.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 3</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 11</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
